    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.surround\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nmini.surround can't work properly with tag ```<router-outlet>```\r\n\r\nAdditionally, when incorporating plugin actions like 'srtt,' the complexity further increases. For instance, in nvim.surround, the tag is going to visiual mode by ```<cst>```, and only the target tag name should be typed.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.5\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n```<router-outlet>*<router-outlet>``` then `<srt>` do not work \r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n```<router-outlet>*<router-outlet>```  `<srt>`\r\n(directly input the target tag name instead of type one more `<t>`)\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nno response",
